<figure class="commit" data-r18-commit aria-labelledby="r18-commit-title">
 <figcaption id="r18-commit-title"><span>Figure 1</span> Which evidence survives the crash?</figcaption>
 <fieldset><legend>Cut the history</legend><label><input type="radio" name="r18-cut" value="0" checked /> Before commit</label><label><input type="radio" name="r18-cut" value="1" /> After durable commit, before reply</label><label><input type="radio" name="r18-cut" value="2" /> After reply</label></fieldset>
 <div class="ledger"><div><strong class="panel-label">Table files</strong><p data-pages data-live>Before purchase: P3 12 · P7 1 · no 103</p></div><div><strong class="panel-label">Durable log</strong><p data-log data-live>No purchase commit record</p></div><div><strong class="panel-label">Application knows</strong><p data-app data-live>Purchase in progress</p></div></div>
 <p data-explanation data-live aria-live="polite">Start before Mina's purchase. No order 103 is present yet.</p>
 <div class="controls" role="group" aria-label="Commit and recovery steps"><button type="button" data-play>Play</button><button type="button" data-back>Back</button><button type="button" data-next>Next</button><button type="button" data-reset>Reset</button><span data-step>1 / 4</span><div data-hold><span></span></div></div>
 <details><summary>Read the three outcomes as text</summary><p>Before a durable commit, no success was promised; this model recovers without the purchase. After a durable commit but before its reply, recovery keeps order 103, both its lines and stock P3 10/P7 0, while the application has an uncertain outcome. After the reply, it keeps that same purchase and the application has received success. In all three histories the table files may still contain older pages before recovery.</p></details>
 <p class="caption">Conceptual cuts, not an observed power failure. The before-commit case deliberately has no surviving commit record; a real connection failure during commit does not reveal which side of the durable boundary it reached.</p>
</figure>
<style>
figure{font-family:var(--font-sans)}figcaption{font-family:var(--font-serif)}

.commit{margin:2rem 0}.commit figcaption{margin-bottom:.7rem;font-size:1.12rem}.commit figcaption span{font:.75rem var(--font-mono);text-transform:uppercase;margin-right:.6rem}.commit fieldset{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.5rem;border:1px solid var(--color-rule);padding:.8rem}.commit legend{font-size:.8rem}.commit label{font-size:.85rem;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.3rem;padding:.3rem}.ledger{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:.6rem;background:var(--color-surface);padding:1rem;border:1px solid var(--color-rule)}.ledger>div{display:grid;grid-template-columns:8rem 1fr;border-left:3px solid var(--color-accent);padding:.5rem .7rem;gap:.75rem}.ledger .panel-label{font:600 .85rem var(--font-mono);margin:0}.ledger p{margin:0;min-height:3rem;font-size:.9rem}.commit>[data-explanation]{min-height:6rem;border-left:3px solid var(--color-accent);padding:.5rem .9rem}.controls{display:flex;gap:.5rem;flex-wrap:wrap;padding:.8rem;background:var(--color-surface);border:1px solid var(--color-rule)}.controls button{font:inherit;color:var(--color-text);background:var(--color-surface);border:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary);padding:.4rem .7rem;cursor:pointer}.controls button:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--color-accent);outline-offset:2px}.controls [aria-disabled=true]{opacity:.55}[data-step]{margin-left:auto;align-self:center;font:.8rem var(--font-mono)}[data-hold]{height:3px;flex-basis:100%;background:var(--color-rule)}[data-hold] span{display:block;height:100%;width:0;background:var(--color-accent)}.caption{font-size:.85rem;color:var(--color-text-secondary)}details{margin:.8rem 0}summary{cursor:pointer}@media(max-width:450px){.ledger{padding:.6rem}.ledger>div{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:.4rem}.ledger p{min-height:3rem}.commit>[data-explanation]{min-height:9rem}}
</style>
<script>
import {stepper} from '../../figures/stepper.mjs';
document.querySelectorAll('[data-r18-commit]').forEach(root=>{
 let cut=0;
 const q=(s:string)=>root.querySelector(s) as HTMLElement;
 const controller=stepper(root,{steps:()=>4,draw(s:number){
  q('[data-pages]').textContent=s===3&&cut>0?'Recovered purchase: P3 10 · P7 0 · 103 and two lines':'Before purchase: P3 12 · P7 1 · no 103';
  q('[data-log]').textContent=s===0?'No purchase commit record':cut===0?'Change records may exist · no commit record':'Purchase changes and commit record flushed';
  q('[data-app]').textContent=s===0?'Purchase in progress':cut===2?'Success received for 103':s>=2?'Connection lost · outcome uncertain':'Waiting for commit reply';
  const captions=["Start before Mina's purchase. No order 103 is present yet.",cut===0?'The transaction changes pages in memory. The model cuts off before any commit record is durable. No success reply has been sent.':cut===1?'The purchase commit record is durable. Table files can still be older. The success reply has not reached the application.':'The purchase commit record is durable and the application has received success. Table pages can still be older.', 'The server crashes. Its private memory disappears. Recovery must use the surviving table files and durable log.',cut===0?'No committed purchase is recovered. Uncommitted versions do not become visible just because their change records were replayed.':'Recovery reconstructs order 103, both lines and stock together. '+(cut===1?'The application still needs to resolve its uncertain request identity.':'The purchase matches the success already received.')];
  q('[data-explanation]').textContent=captions[s];
 }});
 root.querySelectorAll('input').forEach(input=>input.addEventListener('change',()=>{cut=Number((input as HTMLInputElement).value);controller.render();}));
});
</script>
